  "description": "TANLAY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H112 Er4 N12 O16 S6,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.532-3.839 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.49-112.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C154H118Er4N14O16S6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
